## Goal
Follow-ups for the Ask/Remember feature (DEV-50): when "Remember" cannot write the rules file, tell the user with a native macOS notification, and fix a set of related rough edges (IDN host display, lock timeout, JWT unwrap, log tail, docs, tests).

## Problems
None recorded in the session slice. The diff shows the existing failure path was only a `remember failed` line in `decisions.log`, so the user had no visible hint why the next link asked again.

## Decision
- After the link has opened, a failed Remember (both ask panels) posts one notification via a new `internal/handler/notify.go`. `cmd/portero/app.go` builds a one-line body of at most 300 runes with control characters stripped. A fake `notifyFunc` is used in tests.
- The log line gets a suffix such as `(notified)` or `(notification denied)`. A link settled by the unmatched panel logs `none` in the rule column, and the diagram draws it through a "no rule" node.
- The Remember checkbox now says `links from any app`, because the written host rule has no opener condition. IDN hosts are shown in both unicode and punycode forms (`internal/rules/idna.go`), so a look-alike host cannot hide behind one form. The CLI output says that Portero.app would ask.
- The README and `docs/rules.md` warn that older builds reject `default: true` and send every link to Safari. `docs/rules.md` also documents the notification and the 5-second lock timeout.
- ADR 0007 is added with status proposed. The rule file format and the "link opens first" guarantee are unchanged.

